					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-610804#post-1680213</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-610804/rubber-summer#post-1680213</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 07 Jan 2013 15:39:58 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>wishun</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1204404</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Billions of unexplained cubes rain down on the world. Then they start doing things. Some spout jets of flame, some blink like christmas lights, some play &quot;Happy birthday&quot; on a saxophone. Some are deadly, most are not, all are very random. It's all part of an alien plot to conquer Earth with confusion.</p> <p>No, not really. But the mass of sky-objects that do random wierdness, dismissed as silly and turn out to be sinister is the parallel that turned me off.</p> <p>And that pun is <em>really</em> weak.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
